{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/32","id":4502070850,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT3jXmM8AAAABDFgmQg","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/32","diff_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/32.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/32.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/issues/32","number":32,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[ARM64 vNext] Preserve argv semantics and close runtime link mechanics","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Preserve PATH-search errors across `exec*`, `spawn*`, and `posix_spawnp`, so directory candidates report `EACCES` instead of being overwritten by `ENOENT`.\n- Add maintained coverage for same-cohort MSYS operand preservation, native `/dev/urandom` reads, native Windows-child argument conversion, and PATH-search errno behavior.\n- Restore the qualified AArch64 autoload thunk implementation.\n- Preserve real ARM64 `_ctype_`, `fedisableexcept`, and `fegetexcept` exports while excluding x87-only precision interfaces and the x86-only `__alloca` alias.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis branch is stacked on #31 and contains the two qualified post-generator commits `7b711aada` and `846c26818`.\n\nIt intentionally does not modify the separately owned runtime build-reproducibility, linker-rule, `gendef`, TLS, or signal/personality implementation. The integration branch will combine those layers and add the genuine ARM64 `netapi32` and `user32` link inputs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- AArch64 `autoload.o`, `fenv_extern_aarch64.o`, and `ctype_.o` compile with zero error diagnostics.\n- The rebuilt autoload object has 431 global definitions and an exact symbol-set match with the qualified ARM64 object, closing the cited 192-reference autoload bucket.\n- The generated ARM64 definition file is byte-identical to the qualified d70 manifest: 1,763 exports.\n- `libnetapi32.a` contains all 11 required names; `libuser32.a` contains all 38 required names.\n- A private d70-based PE AArch64 runtime links with zero undefined references.\n- Fresh native smoke loads the exact candidate DLL and passes a 64-byte `/dev/urandom` read, a 4096-byte full-block/nonblocking read, `env .` with `EACCES`/126, and fork/wait propagation.\n- The candidate preserves the exact d70 export-name set.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Mechanical source commit: `846c26818d0594f8f872aae9258abb00f52d592a`\n- PATH/argv commit: `7b711aada5077eac6aceaf598eef8d9b4874619a`\n- Mechanical candidate DLL SHA-256: `27491fce530771fcdc13bd41b05a0c619301c6f7793d3e8d3084598042eb7e06`\n- Mechanical handoff SHA-256: `6ce64e609dc49f13aad957943c6b398d34642257a3341f0cad1112929f22e2f2`\n- Sealed d70 baseline DLL SHA-256: `d70cfb46ed6bfa643a6ab557a71008e86043d8a04e5ce2d33549e4e95a49117d`\n\nThe mechanical candidate is proof for this source layer, not a replacement for the separately qualified combined runtime produced by the integration lane.","created_at":"2026-09-11T02:53:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T03:35:47Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"560ea23131b4fd07a7d1d0e